* SUBROUTINE FOR CHARACTER INPUT
READER    EQU   16               Unit number of card reader
INPUT     ORIG  *+16             Place for input cards
NEXTCHAR  STJ   9F               Entrance to subroutine
          JXNZ  3F               Initially rX = 0
1H        J6N   2F               Initially rI6 = 0
          IN    INPUT(READER)    Read next card.
          JBUS  *(READER)        Wait for completion.
          ENN6  16               Let rI6 point to the first word.
2H        LDX   INPUT+16,6       Get the next word of input.
          INC6  1                Advance pointer.
3H        ENTA  0
          SLAX  1                Next character → rA.
9H        JANZ  *                Skip blanks.
          JMP   NEXTCHAR+1
* FIRST COROUTINE
2H        INCA  30               Nondigit found
          JMP   OUT              Send it to OUT coroutine.
IN1       JMP   NEXTCHAR         Get character.
          DECA  30
          JAN   2B               Is it a letter?
          CMPA  =10=
          JGE   2B               Is it a special character?
          STA   *+1(0:2)         Digit n found
          ENT5  *                rI5 ← n.
          JMP   NEXTCHAR         Get next character.
          JMP   OUT              Send it to OUT coroutine.
          DEC5  1                Decrease n by 1.
          J5NN  *-2              Repeat if necessary.
          JMP   IN1              Begin new cycle.
* SECOND COROUTINE
          ALF                    Constant used for blanking
OUTPUT    ORIG  *+16             Buffer area for answers
PUNCH     EQU   17               Unit number for card punch
OUT1      ENT4  -16              Start new output card.
          ENT1  OUTPUT
          MOVE  -1,1(16)         Set output area to blanks.
1H        JMP   IN               Get next translated character.
          STA   OUTPUT+16,4(1:1) Store it in the (1:1) field.
          CMPA  PERIOD           Is it ‘.’?
          JE    9F
          JMP   IN               If not, get another character.
          STA   OUTPUT+16,4(2:2) Store it in the (2:2) field.
          CMPA  PERIOD           Is it ‘.’?
          JE    9F
          JMP   IN               If not, get another character.
          STA   OUTPUT+16,4(3:3) Store it in the (3:3) field.
          CMPA  PERIOD           Is it ‘.’?
          JE    9F
          INC4  1                Move to next word in output buffer.
          J4N   1B               End of card?
9H        OUT   OUTPUT(PUNCH)    If so, punch it.
          JBUS  *(PUNCH)         Wait for completion.
          JNE   OUT1             Return for more, unless
          HLT                    ‘.’ was sensed.
PERIOD    ALF      .
* INITIALIZATION AND LINKAGE
START     ENT6  0                Initialize rI6 for NEXTCHAR.
          ENTX  0                Initialize rX for NEXTCHAR.
          JMP   OUT1             Start with OUT (see exercise 2).
OUT       STJ   INX              Coroutine linkage
OUTX      JMP   OUT1
IN        STJ   OUTX
INX       JMP   IN1
          END   START
